// What the wagons are for (standing loose here: they work the same coupled).
// * Store wagon: stone dropped over it falls in and stays in it. Climbed into (empty paw, right mouse), the wood in
//   paw is stowed in it (right mouse); Space gets out; E takes it all out into the pack.
// * Bunk wagon: climbing in is going to sleep: the wake point moves to it and the game is asked to save. After a death
//   the mole wakes in the tunnel by the bunk wagon, not back where it started.
// * Workshop wagon: outside it there's no workbench and the pickaxe can't be made; inside, it can.
// (bedrock roof: the long room would cave in otherwise)
map
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
#.................................................
#.................................................
#.................................................
#.................................................
#.................................................
#...........@.....................................
##################################################
##################################################
end
mode survival
nohunger
give StoreWagon 1
give BunkWagon 1
give WorkshopWagon 1
give Wood 10
give Stone 12
place 2 -6 0 StoreWagon
place 3 8 0 BunkWagon
place 4 14 0 WorkshopWagon
expect 6 wagons == 3
drop 10 Stone -6 -4
drop 12 Stone -6 -4
expect 120 wagonload == 2             // the stones fell in
use 130 -6 -1                         // climb in
expect 131 inwagon == 1
wield 132 Wood
use 133 -6 -1                         // stow the wood
expect 134 wagonload == 12
expect 134 inv:Wood == 0
hold 140-142 jump                     // out
expect 150 inwagon == 0
pickup 160 -6 0                       // E: unload
expect 161 inv:Wood == 10
expect 161 wagonload == 0
// the bunk
wield 170 none
use 171 8 -1
expect 172 inwagon == 1
expect 172 slept == 1
expect 172 spawnx > 18
expect 172 spawnx < 22
hold 180-182 jump
expect 190 inwagon == 0
// the workshop
craft 200 Pickaxe
expect 201 inv:Pickaxe == 1           // the kit's: no bench here
use 202 14 -1
expect 203 atbench == 1
craft 204 Pickaxe
expect 205 inv:Pickaxe == 2           // made at the wagon's bench
hold 210-212 jump
expect 220 atbench == 0
// a death (the pack is dropped where it fell)...
set 230 hp -5
expect 231 deaths == 1
expect 460 px > 18                    // ...and it wakes by the bunk wagon (at 20), not back at 12
expect 460 px < 23
